+notes='''## Boshsu 1.2 RC5 — Windows discovery and manual updates
+
+Adds a stable Windows AppUserModelID, a Boshsu window name from construction, and optional per-user App Paths / Applications registration with a matching Start-menu shortcut. This makes application identity/path information available through documented Windows mechanisms.
+
+**This is not a certified automatic AMD/Insights game-detection fix.** Those products control their supported-game recognition. No universal client self-registration API was found in the reviewed recorder documentation. AMD's OpenGL recording limitations also remain. [Implementation, research and limits](https://github.com/hsob2nd/Boshsu/blob/main/docs/WINDOWS_DISCOVERY.md).
+
+Registration is enabled on first launch of the packaged build. Use **Options → Advanced → Windows integration** to disable, inspect or repair it; search also finds game detection/recording. It runs outside gameplay, retains foreign entries, and respects which copy owns the current registration. Gameplay, assists, PP and the native engine are unchanged. All RC4 file-picker and RC3 input/UI corrections are retained.
+
+**Manual update:** double-click **Boshsu.Updater.exe**, select your existing installation, downloaded clean ZIP and `SHA256SUMS.txt`, then verify and install. This works offline without the client updater. For an older updater, extract the new ZIP to a separate folder and use its updater to select the existing installation. Keep both downloads from the same official release; local checksums check integrity, not publisher authenticity. Player data is preserved and running targets/downgrades are refused. [Update guide](https://github.com/hsob2nd/Boshsu/blob/main/docs/UPDATES.md).
+
+**In-client update:** Options → Updates → Download → Restart & install, with beta releases enabled. Updating is the player's choice. RC1 users need the complete portable ZIP once; RC2 and later already include the updater.
+
+`Boshsu-1.2-clean.zip` is the complete fresh-data Windows x64 portable beta (.NET Framework 4.8). Extract the whole ZIP and run `Boshsu.exe`. `Boshsu-1.2-source.zip` contains the corresponding source; `SHA256SUMS.txt` provides integrity checks.
+
+Validation: the complete ZIP launched with fresh data, passed 13 first-launch/saved-restart assertions and completed a native gameplay cycle (four pause/resume pairs, one retry and Results). The standalone update window, file selection, full installation and automatic restart passed; 13 tracked player files were unchanged. Tests used disposable data and a launch-only left-monitor override on this Windows PC. Also passed: 29 Windows app-ID/registry/shortcut, 9,736 contract, 2,322 bridge, 5,890 shell and 82 updater checks. These are not all-hardware or recording certifications; capture hooks, automatic recognition and recording performance remain unverified. Your existing installation is updated only when you choose to update it.
+
+User profiles/scores/maps/settings remain independent of application updates. Clean packages exclude private player data and use bounded current-session diagnostics, Off by default. [Full history](https://github.com/hsob2nd/Boshsu/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md).
+
+GPL/MIT/OFL notices and existing supplied-asset/runtime, historical PP, online and platform limitations remain. Support is through GitHub Issues; repository writes/releases remain owner-managed.
+'''
